1
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,200
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,150
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,240
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:39,924 --> 00:00:42,292
<i>You think you're only a flaw in my life?</i>

5
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:45,831
<i>Didn't you ruin that girl's life too?</i>

6
00:00:45,831 --> 00:00:48,324
<i>Woo Soo Bin, you're my one and only regret.</i>

7
00:00:48,324 --> 00:00:52,419
<i>Try going through that day yourself.
See how it feels.</i>

8
00:01:14,438 --> 00:01:16,391
What's wrong?

9
00:01:22,411 --> 00:01:25,504
Is this because of me?

10
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:51,671
Who said it was your fault?

11
00:01:55,537 --> 00:01:57,567
I went there on my own.

12
00:01:57,567 --> 00:01:58,660
You didn't hit me.

13
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,279
- Ju Yi Jae.
- Keep it down.

14
00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:02,578
Your mom just fell asleep.

15
00:02:02,578 --> 00:02:04,446
Let's talk outside.

16
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:14,683
[Episode 6]

17
00:02:17,994 --> 00:02:20,458
Were you never going to tell me?

18
00:02:20,458 --> 00:02:22,976
How could I?

19
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:25,683
If you knew I liked you that much,

20
00:02:25,683 --> 00:02:28,625
you'd get so full of yourself.

21
00:02:28,625 --> 00:02:31,516
So I was never telling you.

22
00:02:31,516 --> 00:02:36,766
You should've slapped me.
Cussed me out, at least.

23
00:02:36,766 --> 00:02:38,511
Don't you remember?

24
00:02:38,511 --> 00:02:39,952
I did all that.

25
00:02:39,952 --> 00:02:42,246
I slapped you and cussed you out.

26
00:02:42,246 --> 00:02:43,797
Ju Yi Jae.

27
00:02:44,384 --> 00:02:47,024
Don't act like it's nothing.

28
00:02:47,621 --> 00:02:50,765
To you, it just happened.

29
00:02:50,765 --> 00:02:53,936
For me, it's been over ten years.

30
00:02:53,936 --> 00:02:57,011
I blamed you plenty.

31
00:02:57,011 --> 00:03:02,294
Without my curses,
you'd be doing a little better by now.

32
00:03:02,294 --> 00:03:04,118
How can you even joke...

33
00:03:04,118 --> 00:03:06,561
I lived with all that ugliness.

34
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:09,374
Then I saw you again, and it hit me.

35
00:03:13,992 --> 00:03:17,326
I'd been blaming myself all along.

36
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:21,256
I couldn't forgive myself.

37
00:03:24,034 --> 00:03:25,859
I told you.

38
00:03:25,859 --> 00:03:27,889
My regret wasn't you.

39
00:03:27,889 --> 00:03:29,105
It was me.

40
00:03:29,105 --> 00:03:30,641
Still...

41
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:33,026
If I hadn't left...

42
00:03:33,026 --> 00:03:34,930
Yeah.

43
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:37,849
Maybe it wouldn't have happened.

44
00:03:37,849 --> 00:03:39,766
So what?

45
00:03:39,766 --> 00:03:42,884
Can you turn back time?

46
00:03:42,884 --> 00:03:45,285
Or erase my memory?

47
00:03:49,451 --> 00:03:51,280
I'll be sorry.

48
00:03:53,097 --> 00:03:55,695
I'll regret it and blame myself.

49
00:03:55,695 --> 00:03:58,937
- This is why I didn't tell...
- Don't ask me not to do that.

50
00:04:01,191 --> 00:04:03,491
That's mine to carry.

51
00:04:37,729 --> 00:04:40,912
Soo Bin, it's not your fault.

52
00:04:42,915 --> 00:04:45,588
It's not your fault.

53
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:50,068
It's okay.

54
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,019
You're up already?

55
00:05:18,019 --> 00:05:20,805
You're awake?

56
00:05:20,805 --> 00:05:23,962
I always wake up at five.

57
00:05:24,817 --> 00:05:26,368
You don't have to cook.

58
00:05:26,368 --> 00:05:28,504
Rest, Mom.

59
00:05:28,504 --> 00:05:31,369
I wanted to.

60
00:05:31,369 --> 00:05:33,166
I'll leave breakfast for you.

61
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,835
Eat whenever you want.

62
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:37,768
- Where are you going?
- Home.

63
00:05:38,529 --> 00:05:42,615
Your father will be up soon.

64
00:05:42,615 --> 00:05:44,240
Mom.

65
00:05:45,673 --> 00:05:47,950
I brought your things.

66
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,854
Just a few clothes for now.

67
00:05:49,854 --> 00:05:53,437
Tell me if you need anything else.

68
00:05:53,437 --> 00:05:55,105
Soo Bin...

69
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:59,863
It's been so long since I had your cooking.

70
00:05:59,863 --> 00:06:02,032
Is this doenjang jjigae?

71
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:10,720
This one with the sun is for the morning.

72
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:13,280
After lunch...

73
00:06:14,844 --> 00:06:18,395
You're usually gardening then,
so I'll draw a flower.

74
00:06:18,395 --> 00:06:20,388
You're a smart one.

75
00:06:20,388 --> 00:06:24,239
If I'd known I'd live this long,
I would've learned to read.

76
00:06:24,239 --> 00:06:25,863
It's not too late.

77
00:06:25,863 --> 00:06:28,016
Why bother? I'll be gone soon.

78
00:06:28,016 --> 00:06:30,945
You said that when I was a student.

79
00:06:31,852 --> 00:06:33,810
Yeah, you're right.

80
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:36,033
The crescent moon is for dinner.

81
00:06:36,033 --> 00:06:38,649
And the one before bed...

82
00:06:38,649 --> 00:06:40,442
A smile!

83
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:43,083
Bedtime is my favorite.

84
00:06:43,083 --> 00:06:45,107
Draw a big smile.

85
00:06:45,107 --> 00:06:46,504
Okay.

86
00:06:46,504 --> 00:06:49,271
[Take before bed if needed]

87
00:06:49,271 --> 00:06:52,516
I'll check when I'm back from Seoul.
Take them, okay?

88
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:54,655
Yeah, I will.

89
00:06:54,655 --> 00:06:58,072
If you fall again,
you could really hurt your back.

90
00:06:58,072 --> 00:06:59,732
Okay.

91
00:07:01,579 --> 00:07:03,209
Mom.

92
00:07:03,209 --> 00:07:06,394
You'll take good care of Grandma, right?

93
00:07:06,394 --> 00:07:07,931
Of course.

94
00:07:07,931 --> 00:07:09,648
Don't worry.

95
00:07:09,648 --> 00:07:12,025
Just focus on your work.

96
00:07:12,025 --> 00:07:14,601
Goodness. Look at your face.

97
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:18,032
How can you care for anyone?

98
00:07:18,032 --> 00:07:20,525
My arms and legs work just fine.

99
00:07:20,525 --> 00:07:23,316
Put me to work.

100
00:07:31,331 --> 00:07:34,261
Good. He had to find out someday.

101
00:07:34,261 --> 00:07:35,439
It's over.

102
00:07:35,439 --> 00:07:36,991
What do you mean, over?

103
00:07:36,991 --> 00:07:39,778
What's he going to do? Go back to America?

104
00:07:39,778 --> 00:07:44,235
He dragged her into this movie.
He'd better see it through.

105
00:07:44,235 --> 00:07:47,860
Well, they'll still make the movie.

106
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:51,303
I mean Soo Bin's heart is done.

107
00:07:51,303 --> 00:07:52,827
What heart?

108
00:07:52,827 --> 00:07:54,313
Love.

109
00:07:54,313 --> 00:07:57,469
- His love.
- Stop talking nonsense.

110
00:07:58,126 --> 00:07:59,723
Hey.

111
00:07:59,723 --> 00:08:02,303
That's the irony of love.

112
00:08:02,303 --> 00:08:05,621
A woman may stay with a man who makes her cry.

113
00:08:05,621 --> 00:08:10,490
But a man can't stay with a woman he made cry.

114
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:13,953
- Why?
- Because it hurts.

115
00:08:13,953 --> 00:08:15,704
It tears him up.

116
00:08:15,704 --> 00:08:19,530
But he can't show his tears.

117
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:22,333
- That's what men are.
- Young Jae...

118
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:24,243
My son.

119
00:08:24,243 --> 00:08:26,482
How did I raise you like this?

120
00:08:26,482 --> 00:08:28,134
All thanks to you, Mom.

121
00:08:28,134 --> 00:08:30,297
That wasn't a compliment.

122
00:08:34,922 --> 00:08:36,301
Hey.

123
00:08:38,288 --> 00:08:41,748
Do you still have pins in your leg?

124
00:08:41,748 --> 00:08:43,993
That's your good morning?

125
00:08:43,993 --> 00:08:45,083
I looked it up.

126
00:08:45,083 --> 00:08:47,599
They probably fixed it with a plate.

127
00:08:47,599 --> 00:08:48,783
Yeah, it's still there.

128
00:08:48,783 --> 00:08:50,963
I'm basically Iron Man.

129
00:08:50,963 --> 00:08:52,429
Why didn't they take it out?

130
00:08:52,429 --> 00:08:53,540
They couldn't.

131
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:57,345
It's too close to the nerves,
so they left it in.

132
00:08:58,671 --> 00:09:00,499
Does it still bother you?

133
00:09:00,499 --> 00:09:02,188
When is it the worst?

134
00:09:02,188 --> 00:09:04,576
- Right now?
- "Right now?"

135
00:09:04,576 --> 00:09:06,996
Let me see. Where?

136
00:09:07,622 --> 00:09:09,759
You wouldn't know by looking.

137
00:09:09,759 --> 00:09:12,469
I need to know how you're doing.

138
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:15,945
It doesn't affect my daily life.

139
00:09:15,945 --> 00:09:17,987
Does it hurt sometimes?

140
00:09:17,987 --> 00:09:21,020
It aches when it rains.

141
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:23,230
And after I walk or run a lot.

142
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:25,106
Especially at night.

143
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,310
Does massage help?

144
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:28,210
Are you taking anything?

145
00:09:28,210 --> 00:09:29,889
Why are you writing that down?

146
00:09:29,889 --> 00:09:31,613
It's not that bad.

147
00:09:31,613 --> 00:09:34,764
How bad is the pain, from zero to ten?

148
00:09:34,764 --> 00:09:37,704
Depends on my mood.

149
00:09:37,704 --> 00:09:40,265
Then I should keep you in a good mood.

150
00:09:40,981 --> 00:09:42,887
Wait.

151
00:09:42,887 --> 00:09:44,639
Then what about that night?

152
00:09:45,239 --> 00:09:47,759
When you kissed me and ran.

153
00:09:51,243 --> 00:09:52,774
<i>What on earth was I thinking?</i>

154
00:09:52,774 --> 00:09:56,169
<i>- Forget it. Don't follow me!
- You're getting soaked!</i>

155
00:09:57,629 --> 00:10:00,625
I couldn't sleep for a lot of reasons.

156
00:10:01,382 --> 00:10:03,066
How bad was it?

157
00:10:03,066 --> 00:10:05,190
On a scale of zero to ten...

158
00:10:07,933 --> 00:10:09,643
Kidding.

159
00:10:09,643 --> 00:10:12,383
So what do you do when it hurts?

160
00:10:12,383 --> 00:10:15,753
I just tough it out. What else?

161
00:10:15,753 --> 00:10:17,548
How do you tough it...

162
00:10:19,198 --> 00:10:20,869
See you later.

163
00:10:33,256 --> 00:10:34,942
Thanks.

164
00:10:56,907 --> 00:10:58,277
What are you doing?

165
00:10:58,277 --> 00:10:59,793
Nothing.

166
00:11:02,019 --> 00:11:04,029
You must've been uncomfortable.

167
00:11:04,029 --> 00:11:06,388
- Huh?
- Just wait.

168
00:11:10,266 --> 00:11:12,043
What's wrong?

169
00:11:12,043 --> 00:11:13,780
I've got it. Don't worry.

170
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:15,008
Hey...

171
00:11:24,368 --> 00:11:26,193
What?

172
00:11:26,193 --> 00:11:28,478
- What is this?
- Where should I put it?

173
00:11:28,478 --> 00:11:30,462
- What?
- You're here. This way.

174
00:11:30,462 --> 00:11:31,973
- Okay.
- Careful.

175
00:11:31,973 --> 00:11:33,285
What is all this?

176
00:11:33,285 --> 00:11:34,911
It's a thing.

177
00:11:35,831 --> 00:11:37,726
Be careful.

178
00:11:42,138 --> 00:11:44,405
I worried for nothing.

179
00:11:44,405 --> 00:11:45,592
Aren't you going to try it?

180
00:11:45,592 --> 00:11:48,924
I read all the reviews. This one's the best.

181
00:11:50,047 --> 00:11:52,064
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

182
00:11:54,335 --> 00:11:57,523
Finally, we finished it!

183
00:11:57,523 --> 00:11:59,229
Nice work.

184
00:11:59,229 --> 00:12:00,642
How did it feel writing again?

185
00:12:00,642 --> 00:12:04,533
Writing is like riding a bike.

186
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:08,936
Once your body remembers,
you don't really forget.

187
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,993
Do I sound kind of obnoxious?

188
00:12:10,993 --> 00:12:14,023
You forgot all that hair-pulling.

189
00:12:14,023 --> 00:12:17,573
I didn't.
And I know this is only the beginning.

190
00:12:17,573 --> 00:12:19,631
So...

191
00:12:19,631 --> 00:12:23,269
Drinks to celebrate the first draft?

192
00:12:23,905 --> 00:12:25,728
I'm in.

193
00:12:25,728 --> 00:12:27,561
[CEO Song from Taebaek]

194
00:12:27,561 --> 00:12:29,204
I'll get it.

195
00:12:33,431 --> 00:12:35,441
I didn't know you had these here.

196
00:12:35,441 --> 00:12:37,131
Yeah?

197
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:40,703
They're like trophies from my reporter days.

198
00:12:40,703 --> 00:12:42,179
You got a lot of awards.

199
00:12:42,179 --> 00:12:45,256
Fine. You pick tonight.

200
00:12:48,755 --> 00:12:49,980
[CEO Song from Taebaek]

201
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,050
I'll go with this.

202
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:53,680
Good choice!

203
00:12:54,623 --> 00:12:56,689
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

204
00:12:59,937 --> 00:13:01,434
Good, right?

205
00:13:01,434 --> 00:13:03,868
Yeah, but it's pretty strong.

206
00:13:03,868 --> 00:13:06,418
I never thought you'd become a reporter.

207
00:13:06,418 --> 00:13:07,915
Neither did I.

208
00:13:07,915 --> 00:13:10,355
How many years was it?

209
00:13:10,355 --> 00:13:13,515
There was this old tree. I climbed it.

210
00:13:13,515 --> 00:13:16,769
I kept it safe so I could steal it later.

211
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:20,532
What's your favorite scene?

212
00:13:20,532 --> 00:13:23,679
Your arrogance,
thinking this one will be a hit too.

213
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:29,087
I never got full of myself
just because I got famous.

214
00:13:29,087 --> 00:13:31,981
You were just too cocky back then.

215
00:14:08,241 --> 00:14:11,870
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

216
00:14:11,870 --> 00:14:14,106
[Screenplay / Director]
[Woo Soo Bin, Ju Yi Jae]

217
00:14:20,290 --> 00:14:21,454
Director Woo.

218
00:14:21,454 --> 00:14:23,430
It looks like a whole new place.

219
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:25,661
What a great studio.

220
00:14:25,661 --> 00:14:28,622
Is this too small for a housewarming gift?

221
00:14:28,622 --> 00:14:29,646
No, thank you.

222
00:14:29,646 --> 00:14:32,848
Even billionaires use toilet paper.

223
00:14:32,848 --> 00:14:36,229
Thank you. Where's the DP?

224
00:14:37,942 --> 00:14:40,286
Hey, Ian!

225
00:14:40,968 --> 00:14:43,819
[Director of Photography]

226
00:14:43,819 --> 00:14:45,608
Hey.

227
00:14:45,608 --> 00:14:47,096
Long time no see.

228
00:14:47,096 --> 00:14:49,056
- What's up?
- You still love gummies?

229
00:14:49,056 --> 00:14:51,724
Can't live without them.

230
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:54,527
Your script made the trip fly by.

231
00:14:54,527 --> 00:14:56,147
You must still be jet-lagged.

232
00:14:56,147 --> 00:14:58,817
Not really. Feels more like a trip.

233
00:14:58,817 --> 00:15:02,361
I've been here before. 20 years ago.

234
00:15:02,361 --> 00:15:05,279
We shot "Silent Waves" here.

235
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:08,436
[Lighting Director]

236
00:15:08,436 --> 00:15:10,096
You scared me.

237
00:15:10,096 --> 00:15:12,037
- You're the lighting director, right?
- Right.

238
00:15:12,037 --> 00:15:15,040
I'm Kim Gwang Il. Even my name shines.

239
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:18,091
Hello, everyone!

240
00:15:18,091 --> 00:15:20,120
I'm Shin Seok Gi, the sound mixer.

241
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,348
[Sound Mixer]

242
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:33,593
[Art Director]

243
00:15:33,593 --> 00:15:36,070
I'm Namgung Se Ra, the art director.

244
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:37,587
Hello.

245
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:41,287
Thank you all for coming all this way.

246
00:15:41,287 --> 00:15:43,654
By the way, where's Director Ju?

247
00:15:43,654 --> 00:15:45,753
Oh, right.

248
00:15:46,783 --> 00:15:49,408
A staff meeting now?

249
00:15:49,408 --> 00:15:52,048
I'm not ready for this.

250
00:15:53,374 --> 00:15:56,988
Why can't this thing find the location?

251
00:15:57,999 --> 00:15:59,612
Excuse me.

252
00:16:01,747 --> 00:16:03,104
Excuse me.

253
00:16:03,104 --> 00:16:04,840
Sorry...

254
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,625
- What do you want?
- Directions!

255
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:08,009
I just wanted directions!

256
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:11,200
- Who asks strangers for directions now?
- I'm serious!

257
00:16:12,217 --> 00:16:14,225
Director Ju Yi Jae?

258
00:16:14,904 --> 00:16:16,747
Who are you?

259
00:16:16,747 --> 00:16:20,338
[Assistant Director]

260
00:16:20,338 --> 00:16:23,918
I'm Ryu Sang Mok, the assistant director.

261
00:16:24,935 --> 00:16:27,180
- I'm so sorry, sir.
- Oh my.

262
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:29,435
- You okay?
- That hurts...

263
00:16:30,551 --> 00:16:32,492
You touched me out of nowhere...

264
00:16:32,492 --> 00:16:34,678
- You twisted my arm out of nowhere.
- Sorry...

265
00:16:36,255 --> 00:16:38,332
- This way, please.
- Thanks.

266
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:40,042
Hello.

267
00:16:40,042 --> 00:16:41,555
- You're here.
- Hello.

268
00:16:41,555 --> 00:16:45,213
- The parking lot's far, huh?
- Yes. I got totally lost.

269
00:16:45,213 --> 00:16:48,116
I ran into Director Ju right out front.

270
00:16:52,247 --> 00:16:54,623
Hello. Nice to meet you.

271
00:16:54,623 --> 00:16:57,317
I'm Ju Yi Jae.

272
00:16:57,317 --> 00:16:59,428
At least we got to meet you.

273
00:16:59,428 --> 00:17:00,562
Good to see you.

274
00:17:00,562 --> 00:17:05,165
Maybe we should save introductions
until after location scouting.

275
00:17:05,165 --> 00:17:06,488
We should hurry.

276
00:17:06,488 --> 00:17:09,200
- No time to waste.
- Let's go.

277
00:17:10,594 --> 00:17:12,178
See you later.

278
00:17:12,178 --> 00:17:15,021
You're location scouting now?

279
00:17:16,453 --> 00:17:19,180
Hold on a second, please.

280
00:17:23,572 --> 00:17:25,226
Just a second.

281
00:17:31,045 --> 00:17:32,636
What?

282
00:17:32,636 --> 00:17:34,909
Weren't we having a script meeting today?

283
00:17:34,909 --> 00:17:36,098
Yeah.

284
00:17:36,098 --> 00:17:39,110
While I'm location scouting,
you can meet with the producers.

285
00:17:39,110 --> 00:17:41,376
Why am I being left out?

286
00:17:41,376 --> 00:17:43,820
We can split things up.

287
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:45,816
You said we'd do everything together.

288
00:17:45,816 --> 00:17:48,777
If you're scouting locations,
you'll probably be hiking.

289
00:17:48,777 --> 00:17:52,433
Are you leaving me out because of my leg?

290
00:17:52,433 --> 00:17:54,115
That's not it.

291
00:17:54,115 --> 00:17:55,449
We're checking sets too.

292
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,895
- That's not what I mean.
- Yi Jae.

293
00:17:58,495 --> 00:18:00,792
I think this is for the best.

294
00:18:02,515 --> 00:18:05,781
Let's just do it this way. Okay?

295
00:18:07,355 --> 00:18:08,840
I'm off.

296
00:18:17,309 --> 00:18:19,179
How many steps today?

297
00:18:19,179 --> 00:18:22,266
Who knows? We'll easily pass 30,000.

298
00:18:22,266 --> 00:18:24,617
- Is he joking?
- Huh?

299
00:18:24,617 --> 00:18:27,251
- Dead serious.
- Jeez.

300
00:18:27,251 --> 00:18:31,006
My knees are already killing me.
Must be nice to skip this.

301
00:18:31,006 --> 00:18:35,819
But location scouting is
the heart of pre-production.

302
00:18:35,819 --> 00:18:38,499
It's an honor to join you, sir.

303
00:18:38,499 --> 00:18:41,523
Hey. If it hurts, sit this one out.

304
00:18:41,523 --> 00:18:43,547
I wouldn't miss it.

305
00:18:43,547 --> 00:18:47,247
Come on. Why would you say that?

306
00:18:47,247 --> 00:18:49,030
Gwang Il's feelings are hurt.

307
00:18:49,030 --> 00:18:52,089
- Have a safe trip.
- See you later.

308
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:55,042
Have a good talk.

309
00:18:56,183 --> 00:18:58,907
Call me if anything comes up.

310
00:18:58,907 --> 00:19:01,793
- Okay.
- Don't worry.

311
00:19:01,793 --> 00:19:04,558
- Have a safe trip.
- Bye.

312
00:19:13,591 --> 00:19:16,149
We organized the scene list like this.

313
00:19:16,149 --> 00:19:17,658
- Next is...
- Here.

314
00:19:17,658 --> 00:19:18,948
Yeah.

315
00:19:29,525 --> 00:19:33,885
Next, I'll go over the directing team's notes.

316
00:19:55,288 --> 00:19:57,118
Are you okay?

317
00:20:01,797 --> 00:20:04,654
You should go to a hospital.

318
00:20:04,654 --> 00:20:06,798
I'm okay.

319
00:20:25,976 --> 00:20:27,646
<i>Did you die on the way?</i>

320
00:20:27,646 --> 00:20:30,911
<i>What took you so long?</i>

321
00:20:30,911 --> 00:20:32,664
<i>The accident report is filed.</i>

322
00:20:32,664 --> 00:20:36,908
<i>This order will be refunded,
so there's no delivery fee.</i>

323
00:20:38,089 --> 00:20:40,627
<i>You okay? Are you badly hurt?</i>

324
00:20:40,627 --> 00:20:42,301
<i>What about repairs?</i>

325
00:20:42,301 --> 00:20:44,595
<i>I can lend you money.</i>

326
00:21:37,245 --> 00:21:38,731
So salty.

327
00:21:43,769 --> 00:21:46,370
This is what you asked for.

328
00:21:50,029 --> 00:21:51,280
So...

329
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:54,210
The guy Ha Na was looking for...

330
00:21:54,210 --> 00:21:56,604
and the one from the shin incident...

331
00:21:57,257 --> 00:22:00,457
- they're both him?
- Yes, ma'am.

332
00:22:06,708 --> 00:22:08,455
Interesting.

333
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:17,280
The soup was too salty today.

334
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:19,285
Ma'am...

335
00:22:21,419 --> 00:22:23,912
She ate it all, then talked crap.

336
00:22:37,777 --> 00:22:39,307
Hey.

337
00:22:39,307 --> 00:22:41,114
[The Woman with Shaky Guts, The Man with Shaky Hands]
Are you doing this?

338
00:22:41,114 --> 00:22:44,317
I hear CEO An is bending over
backward for Director Kim,

339
00:22:44,317 --> 00:22:47,541
trying to get you cast as Shaky Guts.

340
00:22:47,541 --> 00:22:50,245
Your mother must be working hard.

341
00:22:50,245 --> 00:22:52,295
Maybe she'll send burgers next.

342
00:22:52,295 --> 00:22:55,478
This is too childish to listen to.

343
00:22:56,262 --> 00:22:57,719
So what?

344
00:22:57,719 --> 00:22:59,338
"So what?"

345
00:22:59,338 --> 00:23:02,928
I got dropped because of you.
I was Shaky Hands!

346
00:23:02,928 --> 00:23:07,132
Everyone heard we fought, and now I'm screwed.

347
00:23:07,132 --> 00:23:09,254
You were already screwed.

348
00:23:10,813 --> 00:23:13,310
I was up for this first.

349
00:23:13,310 --> 00:23:16,316
I'd already met with the director.

350
00:23:16,316 --> 00:23:20,234
I haven't even read the script yet.
Isn't that your problem?

351
00:23:20,234 --> 00:23:24,014
What? I heard you even wrote the director
a handwritten letter.

352
00:23:24,014 --> 00:23:25,711
What the hell?

353
00:23:26,977 --> 00:23:29,272
So that was CEO An's plan too?

354
00:23:29,272 --> 00:23:33,508
No wonder you're in your own bubble
while it's war out here.

355
00:23:33,508 --> 00:23:35,123
Lucky you.

356
00:23:35,123 --> 00:23:38,075
The world must look so pretty to you.

357
00:23:38,075 --> 00:23:39,878
Then take it. It's yours.

358
00:23:39,878 --> 00:23:42,481
Take what? CEO An?

359
00:23:47,038 --> 00:23:49,603
Shaky Hands. You take it.

360
00:23:49,603 --> 00:23:52,312
I'm not staying here anyway.

361
00:23:53,369 --> 00:23:55,020
I'm getting out.

362
00:23:55,020 --> 00:23:57,653
What are you talking about?

363
00:23:57,653 --> 00:24:00,479
You're skipping the wrap party?

364
00:24:01,126 --> 00:24:03,217
- Are you an idiot?
- Yeah.

365
00:24:03,217 --> 00:24:05,397
- Get out.
- You mean it?

366
00:24:05,397 --> 00:24:06,954
I'm doing this show.

367
00:24:06,954 --> 00:24:08,894
You sure?

368
00:24:08,894 --> 00:24:11,977
No taking it back later!

369
00:24:18,247 --> 00:24:20,770
Group photo! Everyone gather up!

370
00:24:20,770 --> 00:24:23,552
- Hurry!
- Everyone, get ready.

371
00:24:23,552 --> 00:24:25,013
Let's take it.

372
00:24:27,968 --> 00:24:30,177
Who are you looking for?

373
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:32,434
Where did Yu Geon go?

374
00:24:32,434 --> 00:24:35,067
Yu Geon? Who's that?

375
00:24:35,067 --> 00:24:36,257
Gang Member Number 3.

376
00:24:36,257 --> 00:24:38,228
Oh, him?

377
00:24:38,228 --> 00:24:40,541
He died.

378
00:24:40,541 --> 00:24:42,328
When?

379
00:24:42,328 --> 00:24:44,328
On your day off.

380
00:24:46,927 --> 00:24:48,740
I see.

381
00:25:04,031 --> 00:25:07,400
Come back home already.

382
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:09,641
You've done enough.

383
00:25:09,641 --> 00:25:12,968
Come learn the business.

384
00:25:12,968 --> 00:25:15,579
It's been two years.

385
00:25:16,815 --> 00:25:19,719
Can't you ask how I've been?

386
00:25:19,719 --> 00:25:25,587
Am I asking you to care for me?
Or bring home money?

387
00:25:25,587 --> 00:25:27,229
Just take over the shop.

388
00:25:27,229 --> 00:25:29,436
I said I don't want to.

389
00:25:29,436 --> 00:25:31,653
Then why do deliveries?

390
00:25:31,653 --> 00:25:36,657
Every motorcycle accident on the news
makes my heart drop!

391
00:25:37,324 --> 00:25:43,125
What you're doing isn't perseverance.
It's stubbornness.

392
00:25:43,125 --> 00:25:44,840
No.

393
00:25:45,691 --> 00:25:48,187
I can do this.

394
00:25:48,187 --> 00:25:52,124
I don't want to end up with a regret
like your guitar.

395
00:25:53,813 --> 00:25:55,669
Why did you come?

396
00:25:56,626 --> 00:25:59,063
To tear me apart?

397
00:26:00,332 --> 00:26:02,271
I just...

398
00:26:04,865 --> 00:26:07,605
missed you, Dad.

399
00:26:17,411 --> 00:26:20,044
But I need to say this before I go.

400
00:26:21,231 --> 00:26:22,982
I'm...

401
00:26:24,378 --> 00:26:27,846
I'm not quitting. I can't quit.

402
00:26:29,666 --> 00:26:31,546
I'm sorry, Dad.

403
00:26:36,346 --> 00:26:38,352
That little...

404
00:26:46,250 --> 00:26:48,894
You have one month left!

405
00:26:48,894 --> 00:26:53,882
If you don't come back,
I'll drag you back myself!

406
00:27:43,247 --> 00:27:46,562
He's just worried about you.

407
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:52,298
He watches everything you're in.

408
00:27:52,298 --> 00:27:55,698
I don't even know where you show up,
but he knows it all.

409
00:27:55,698 --> 00:27:58,475
"Close-up and down, bust!"

410
00:27:58,475 --> 00:28:00,587
He even knows your lines.

411
00:28:00,587 --> 00:28:02,629
What's the point?

412
00:28:02,629 --> 00:28:04,818
All he ever says is to quit.

413
00:28:05,439 --> 00:28:08,376
Come on. You're Sim Yu Geon, Takeshi Kaneshiro.

414
00:28:08,376 --> 00:28:11,769
The town heartthrob can't look this gloomy.

415
00:28:11,769 --> 00:28:14,029
Takeshi Kaneshiro, my ass.

416
00:28:14,656 --> 00:28:18,799
Seoul is full of good-looking guys.

417
00:28:18,799 --> 00:28:20,617
Don't lie.

418
00:28:20,617 --> 00:28:23,196
Think I don't know Seoul?

419
00:28:23,196 --> 00:28:25,482
I can talk Seoul too.

420
00:28:27,296 --> 00:28:29,458
"Have you eaten?"

421
00:28:29,458 --> 00:28:30,926
Stop it.

422
00:28:30,926 --> 00:28:32,375
Just watch the road.

423
00:28:32,375 --> 00:28:33,886
"Have you eaten?"

424
00:28:35,343 --> 00:28:37,634
[Bunam Intercity Bus Terminal]

425
00:28:37,634 --> 00:28:40,248
We're here. Get out.

426
00:28:40,248 --> 00:28:41,942
Thanks.

427
00:28:43,869 --> 00:28:45,451
Oh, right.

428
00:28:45,451 --> 00:28:46,929
Here.

429
00:28:48,422 --> 00:28:50,921
- What is it?
- It's from your dad.

430
00:28:53,062 --> 00:28:54,446
I'm off.

431
00:28:54,446 --> 00:28:56,890
Hey! Ju Young Jae!

432
00:29:16,641 --> 00:29:17,758
Hello?

433
00:29:17,758 --> 00:29:21,584
<i>Hello, is this Sim Yu Geon?</i>

434
00:29:21,584 --> 00:29:23,535
Yes, it is.

435
00:29:23,535 --> 00:29:25,235
Who is this?

436
00:29:25,235 --> 00:29:27,588
<i>It's me. Director Kang.</i>

437
00:29:38,027 --> 00:29:40,944
That location manager is driving me crazy.

438
00:29:40,944 --> 00:29:43,775
I told him this place wasn't ideal.

439
00:29:43,775 --> 00:29:46,453
We'd need at least ten assistants.

440
00:29:46,453 --> 00:29:48,497
It'll blow up the budget.

441
00:29:48,497 --> 00:29:49,706
Exactly.

442
00:29:49,706 --> 00:29:52,493
I bet he left it on the list on purpose.

443
00:29:52,493 --> 00:29:54,923
He knew they'd say yes to that place.

444
00:29:54,923 --> 00:29:56,947
He just didn't want to hit more spots.

445
00:29:56,947 --> 00:29:59,824
That's seriously shady.

446
00:29:59,824 --> 00:30:01,537
Director Ju.

447
00:30:01,537 --> 00:30:04,048
Could you talk to him?

448
00:30:04,048 --> 00:30:05,355
Me?

449
00:30:06,942 --> 00:30:09,932
I think I'm missing some context.

450
00:30:09,932 --> 00:30:11,265
Sorry?

451
00:30:12,314 --> 00:30:15,185
The photos in the chat...

452
00:30:22,105 --> 00:30:24,922
Oh, she's not in the chat.

453
00:30:24,922 --> 00:30:26,773
She's not.

454
00:30:28,989 --> 00:30:30,787
What?

455
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:34,095
You're not in this group chat?

456
00:30:34,095 --> 00:30:35,995
No.

457
00:30:35,995 --> 00:30:37,591
I'm sorry.

458
00:30:37,591 --> 00:30:40,310
- Director Ryu made this chat, huh?
- Yes.

459
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:42,783
I'll add you right now.

460
00:30:42,783 --> 00:30:45,012
No, it's okay.

461
00:30:45,012 --> 00:30:48,640
Director Woo probably thought
it would distract me from writing.

462
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,475
I'll get the updates from him separately.

463
00:30:50,475 --> 00:30:53,518
That makes sense.

464
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:55,480
I panicked for nothing.

465
00:30:56,321 --> 00:30:58,024
Gosh...

466
00:30:58,911 --> 00:31:00,756
Anyway...

467
00:31:03,132 --> 00:31:05,990
We'll head out now.

468
00:31:05,990 --> 00:31:08,114
Isn't the commute annoying?

469
00:31:08,114 --> 00:31:10,787
You can sleep here if you'd like.

470
00:31:10,787 --> 00:31:14,036
Oh, no. Please make yourself comfortable.

471
00:31:14,036 --> 00:31:16,290
Our lodging is close.

472
00:31:16,290 --> 00:31:19,230
I live nearby too...

473
00:31:19,230 --> 00:31:20,774
See you tomorrow.

474
00:31:20,774 --> 00:31:22,466
Good night.

475
00:31:22,466 --> 00:31:23,744
Yeah.

476
00:31:23,744 --> 00:31:25,751
- See you tomorrow.
- Good work.

477
00:31:25,751 --> 00:31:27,176
Good work.

478
00:31:37,658 --> 00:31:39,775
- What was that?
- That wasn't funny.

479
00:31:39,775 --> 00:31:42,679
Don't make jokes like that.

480
00:31:47,562 --> 00:31:48,919
Oh, hi.

481
00:31:48,919 --> 00:31:51,632
We were just on our way to the lodging...

482
00:31:51,632 --> 00:31:53,789
I see.

483
00:31:53,789 --> 00:31:55,409
Want to join us?

484
00:31:55,409 --> 00:31:57,532
- One second.
- Here...

485
00:31:59,397 --> 00:32:01,338
- Hello.
<i>- Hey.</i>

486
00:32:01,338 --> 00:32:02,841
We're getting chicken...

487
00:32:02,841 --> 00:32:04,505
Sure, I'm on my way.

488
00:32:04,505 --> 00:32:07,065
<i>- What?</i>
- I actually have plans too.

489
00:32:07,065 --> 00:32:08,776
<i>You're in?</i>

490
00:32:08,776 --> 00:32:10,441
Yes. Order first.

491
00:32:10,441 --> 00:32:12,182
<i>You have to order it.</i>

492
00:32:12,182 --> 00:32:13,777
<i>Fried one?</i>

493
00:32:17,275 --> 00:32:18,959
Chicken?

494
00:32:18,959 --> 00:32:20,983
What chicken?

495
00:32:20,983 --> 00:32:22,983
You didn't order?

496
00:32:25,386 --> 00:32:28,402
What's with her now?

497
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:41,236
My legs are killing me.

498
00:32:49,786 --> 00:32:51,124
Everyone.

499
00:32:51,124 --> 00:32:54,157
I know you're tired, but let's meet briefly.

500
00:32:54,157 --> 00:32:56,157
This can't go on.

501
00:33:03,813 --> 00:33:04,838
Let's go.

502
00:33:04,838 --> 00:33:06,322
[Munak Mountain]

503
00:33:06,322 --> 00:33:10,172
After all these days,
are these really our best options?

504
00:33:10,172 --> 00:33:13,043
I know period pieces are hard on this budget.

505
00:33:13,043 --> 00:33:17,082
But I don't want to settle
and fix it with tricks in post.

506
00:33:17,082 --> 00:33:20,052
Yeah, right.

507
00:33:20,052 --> 00:33:22,063
We have standards.

508
00:33:22,063 --> 00:33:24,004
Let's keep looking.

509
00:33:24,004 --> 00:33:25,482
We need more legwork.

510
00:33:25,482 --> 00:33:28,666
Director Ryu,
let's check around the sets again.

511
00:33:28,666 --> 00:33:30,976
No residents. No tourists.

512
00:33:30,976 --> 00:33:32,669
No power lines...

513
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:40,317
No power lines. Good natural light.

514
00:33:40,317 --> 00:33:43,474
- You know what I mean.
- I do, but...

515
00:33:43,474 --> 00:33:46,548
You said exposed places won't work either.

516
00:33:46,548 --> 00:33:48,669
- Then there really isn't anywhere.
- No.

517
00:33:48,669 --> 00:33:52,649
Either it exists, or we haven't found it.

518
00:33:52,649 --> 00:33:53,799
Next slide.

519
00:33:53,799 --> 00:33:55,482
Director Ju.

520
00:33:56,209 --> 00:33:57,913
You're here.

521
00:33:57,913 --> 00:34:01,041
Weren't you coming tomorrow?

522
00:34:01,041 --> 00:34:06,506
The landowner suddenly backed out,
so they came back.

523
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:08,720
Yeah.

524
00:34:09,526 --> 00:34:12,467
This place is too tight.

525
00:34:26,603 --> 00:34:28,827
Where is everyone?

526
00:34:28,827 --> 00:34:31,733
The lodging. I sent them off.

527
00:34:32,473 --> 00:34:34,719
Why? You want to be alone?

528
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:36,957
- Should I leave too?
- No.

529
00:34:36,957 --> 00:34:38,928
I wanted us to be alone.

530
00:34:38,928 --> 00:34:40,568
How was the meeting?

531
00:34:40,568 --> 00:34:41,915
Well...

532
00:34:43,110 --> 00:34:46,518
You haven't seen the photos yet, right?

533
00:34:52,973 --> 00:34:56,794
This one's great,
but cars can't get in, so it's out.

534
00:34:56,794 --> 00:35:00,071
This one looked good,
but there wasn't enough space.

535
00:35:00,071 --> 00:35:01,935
This one's the best so far.

536
00:35:01,935 --> 00:35:03,421
What do you think?

537
00:35:09,821 --> 00:35:12,310
Do you even want my opinion?

538
00:35:13,620 --> 00:35:17,258
- What?
- If I don't, I shake my head?

539
00:35:17,258 --> 00:35:19,283
What do you want?

540
00:35:19,283 --> 00:35:20,949
I'll do whatever you say.

541
00:35:20,949 --> 00:35:22,055
What's wrong?

542
00:35:22,055 --> 00:35:25,492
You saw them in person
and you're still not sure.

543
00:35:25,492 --> 00:35:27,882
So what would I know?

544
00:35:28,536 --> 00:35:31,795
I can barely face the staff who worked so hard.

545
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:36,765
- I cleared it with everyone, so...
- What did you say?

546
00:35:36,765 --> 00:35:38,722
"Yi Jae is my first love?"

547
00:35:38,722 --> 00:35:42,818
"She's special to me,
so please be considerate?"

548
00:35:42,818 --> 00:35:46,545
Or... "Her leg is bad because of me.

549
00:35:46,545 --> 00:35:49,710
So leave her out of the hard stuff?"

550
00:35:49,710 --> 00:35:51,162
Why?

551
00:35:51,162 --> 00:35:53,042
- Did someone say something?
- No.

552
00:35:53,042 --> 00:35:54,444
Nobody said anything.

553
00:35:54,444 --> 00:35:56,406
Isn't that weird?

554
00:35:56,406 --> 00:36:00,929
No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.

555
00:36:04,385 --> 00:36:06,338
Why do you think?

556
00:36:12,284 --> 00:36:14,115
Yi Jae.

557
00:36:14,115 --> 00:36:16,097
Ju Yi Jae!

558
00:36:27,763 --> 00:36:30,801
Why am I crying?

559
00:36:30,801 --> 00:36:33,633
I didn't even cry when I won the Grand Prize.

560
00:36:36,260 --> 00:36:38,909
Why is this so sad?

561
00:36:44,750 --> 00:36:47,952
[Gyeongseong Love Song]
But do things like this sell these days?

562
00:36:49,637 --> 00:36:50,872
Ma'am.

563
00:36:50,872 --> 00:36:52,247
Yes?

564
00:36:53,257 --> 00:36:55,267
The car is ready.

565
00:36:56,399 --> 00:36:58,842
How do I look today?

566
00:36:58,842 --> 00:37:00,183
Were you yawning?

567
00:37:00,183 --> 00:37:01,872
Darn it.

568
00:37:04,037 --> 00:37:05,879
Look closer.

569
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:08,674
Forget it. Just give me the contract.

570
00:37:08,674 --> 00:37:09,869
Yes, ma'am.

571
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:15,546
It's been a while. I'm kind of excited.

572
00:37:15,546 --> 00:37:17,341
- Let's go!
- Okay.

573
00:37:26,322 --> 00:37:27,970
- Let's go.
- Yes.

574
00:37:42,046 --> 00:37:44,952
Looks like she's leaving now.

575
00:37:44,952 --> 00:37:46,545
Okay.

576
00:38:18,376 --> 00:38:19,883
[Oh Ha Na]

577
00:38:30,308 --> 00:38:32,151
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

578
00:38:49,490 --> 00:38:51,165
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

579
00:38:51,930 --> 00:38:54,077
"Gyeongseong Love Song?"

580
00:39:10,726 --> 00:39:15,123
"A single ray of moonlight
falls over Wolhajeong.

581
00:39:15,123 --> 00:39:18,914
Nan Young stands in the heart of the darkness."

582
00:39:28,296 --> 00:39:30,176
Nan Young.

583
00:39:30,176 --> 00:39:35,187
After catching her breath,
she sets down the heavy bag in her hand

584
00:39:35,187 --> 00:39:37,620
and takes something out.

585
00:39:38,412 --> 00:39:42,480
In her trembling hand is a stick of dynamite.

586
00:39:45,065 --> 00:39:47,504
Her mind is already made up.

587
00:39:48,144 --> 00:39:51,050
The moment she lights this fuse,

588
00:39:51,840 --> 00:39:54,534
everything will begin.

589
00:39:57,267 --> 00:40:00,857
After hiding explosives all over Wolhajeong,

590
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:03,540
she stands there, gripping the fuse tight.

591
00:40:04,193 --> 00:40:09,843
Below the wall,
her face flickers red in the match light.

592
00:40:15,267 --> 00:40:19,652
Tonight, she will blow up Wolhajeong.

593
00:40:20,714 --> 00:40:22,324
<i>Now I finally understand.</i>

594
00:40:22,324 --> 00:40:26,401
<i>Wolhajeong's high walls
were never fences that protected me.</i>

595
00:40:26,401 --> 00:40:29,541
<i>They were bars that kept me locked away.</i>

596
00:40:29,541 --> 00:40:33,361
<i>Now, with my own hands,
I will tear it all down.</i>

597
00:40:49,854 --> 00:40:51,918
Let's go.

598
00:40:57,540 --> 00:41:00,772
<i>I found my way out.</i>

599
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:06,222
Make yourself comfortable.

600
00:41:08,706 --> 00:41:12,385
No, it's okay.

601
00:41:14,863 --> 00:41:16,430
So...

602
00:41:17,637 --> 00:41:19,762
Have you decided?

603
00:41:20,524 --> 00:41:22,974
I'm not a patient woman.

604
00:41:23,797 --> 00:41:27,901
I want to make it, CEO An.

605
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:31,761
Can that happen...

606
00:41:32,934 --> 00:41:34,636
in a month?

607
00:41:37,202 --> 00:41:39,686
I told you, I'm impatient.

608
00:41:42,992 --> 00:41:45,874
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

609
00:41:59,298 --> 00:42:01,684
How does it feel today?

610
00:42:02,798 --> 00:42:06,963
It feels real, but also like a dream.

611
00:42:07,971 --> 00:42:13,173
But it's our first crew dinner,
and In Uk still didn't show.

612
00:42:13,173 --> 00:42:15,646
He has a dating show today.

613
00:42:15,646 --> 00:42:18,511
- A dating show?
- A romance reality show.

614
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,584
What is he even doing?

615
00:42:22,584 --> 00:42:25,879
Well, as long as we have the company card.

616
00:42:25,879 --> 00:42:29,001
He said you'd be paying.

617
00:42:29,001 --> 00:42:32,640
- Me?
- He said to keep the receipts.

618
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:35,622
Is he trying to ruin my credit?

619
00:42:37,487 --> 00:42:39,733
There's Director Ju.

620
00:42:41,133 --> 00:42:42,871
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

621
00:42:42,871 --> 00:42:44,708
- Hello.
- Hello.

622
00:42:44,708 --> 00:42:46,816
- You're here.
- Hello.

623
00:43:10,564 --> 00:43:13,688
Director Seo is shooting on the island, right?

624
00:43:13,688 --> 00:43:15,228
Isn't that close?

625
00:43:15,228 --> 00:43:19,218
Don't even think about going.
It's a mess over there.

626
00:43:19,218 --> 00:43:22,022
One wrong move, and you're stuck there too.

627
00:43:22,022 --> 00:43:27,274
It's basically a prison camp.
The crew's ready to build a raft and escape.

628
00:43:27,274 --> 00:43:30,399
You mean Director Seo Dong Yun?

629
00:43:30,399 --> 00:43:33,033
He's famous for being strict.

630
00:43:33,033 --> 00:43:37,033
I heard his sets
are some of the toughest around.

631
00:43:40,390 --> 00:43:42,080
Director Ju.

632
00:43:42,080 --> 00:43:44,827
I guess you're not tough.

633
00:43:44,827 --> 00:43:47,972
Directors are supposed to be strict.

634
00:43:47,972 --> 00:43:50,599
That's how Director Seo got this far.

635
00:43:50,599 --> 00:43:54,991
Anyone who survives that set
wears it like a badge.

636
00:43:54,991 --> 00:43:57,999
Right. It becomes pride.

637
00:43:58,981 --> 00:44:02,111
Art Director, there you are.

638
00:44:02,111 --> 00:44:05,328
Why are you sitting here?

639
00:44:05,328 --> 00:44:08,302
You went to Seonghwa Arts College, right?

640
00:44:08,302 --> 00:44:10,610
Can I call you senior?

641
00:44:10,610 --> 00:44:12,931
Just call me Se Ra.

642
00:44:12,931 --> 00:44:14,388
Yes, Se Ra.

643
00:44:14,388 --> 00:44:18,241
I'm Ryu Sang Mok,
Seonghwa Theater and Film, class of '02.

644
00:44:18,241 --> 00:44:20,265
I was never that attached to my school.

645
00:44:20,265 --> 00:44:23,171
Then get attached to me.

646
00:44:23,171 --> 00:44:25,123
- Excuse me!
- Huh?

647
00:44:25,123 --> 00:44:28,003
Who are you talking to?

648
00:44:36,895 --> 00:44:38,966
Director Ju.

649
00:44:39,661 --> 00:44:42,004
Where did you go to college?

650
00:44:42,893 --> 00:44:47,522
Why did you become a reporter
instead of using your major?

651
00:44:49,194 --> 00:44:51,661
- I...
- Cheers!

652
00:44:53,017 --> 00:44:54,448
Raise your glass.

653
00:44:54,448 --> 00:44:56,589
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

654
00:45:07,071 --> 00:45:10,454
Is life seriously this unfair?

655
00:45:10,454 --> 00:45:12,124
Tell me about it.

656
00:45:12,124 --> 00:45:16,417
Some people grind for 13 years
and still never debut.

657
00:45:16,417 --> 00:45:19,142
Hey, Mr. Five Years.

658
00:45:19,142 --> 00:45:21,876
That number was pretty specific.

659
00:45:21,876 --> 00:45:23,474
Are you talking about me?

660
00:45:23,474 --> 00:45:28,309
I mean, with veterans like you still waiting...

661
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:31,427
- And some total nobody... huh?
- Yeah.

662
00:45:31,427 --> 00:45:33,620
Exactly.

663
00:45:33,620 --> 00:45:36,140
Darn it.

664
00:45:36,963 --> 00:45:38,941
I need to pee.

665
00:45:40,673 --> 00:45:43,310
But this is too much!

666
00:45:43,310 --> 00:45:46,231
She's a former reporter.

667
00:45:46,231 --> 00:45:49,229
Fine. I can let that slide.

668
00:45:49,229 --> 00:45:50,533
But what?

669
00:45:50,533 --> 00:45:52,377
She's never even studied film.

670
00:45:52,377 --> 00:45:56,309
Plenty of directors didn't study film.

671
00:45:56,309 --> 00:45:58,333
Come on!

672
00:45:58,333 --> 00:46:01,441
There are levels to that.

673
00:46:01,441 --> 00:46:06,241
It's not like she went
to Korea University or Harvard.

674
00:46:06,241 --> 00:46:09,811
How does some no-name college grad
just waltz in?

675
00:46:09,811 --> 00:46:11,171
Calm down.

676
00:46:11,171 --> 00:46:14,108
What's taking so long? Huh?

677
00:46:14,108 --> 00:46:18,733
- Calm down.
- I'll kick this door down.

678
00:46:20,030 --> 00:46:21,444
- No, no.
- Darn it.

679
00:46:21,444 --> 00:46:23,546
Calm down.

680
00:46:25,533 --> 00:46:27,243
Hey! Come out already!

681
00:46:27,243 --> 00:46:30,402
- Hold on.
- Come out! Hey!

682
00:46:30,402 --> 00:46:32,349
- Calm down.
- Do you know who I am?

683
00:46:32,349 --> 00:46:34,962
- Calm down, sir.
- What the...

684
00:46:34,962 --> 00:46:37,130
I'm sorry.

685
00:46:37,130 --> 00:46:39,056
Director Ju?

686
00:46:49,476 --> 00:46:52,271
She heard you! Jeez...

687
00:46:52,271 --> 00:46:54,105
It's true, though!

688
00:46:54,105 --> 00:46:56,158
- Yi Jae.
- You need the bathroom?

689
00:46:56,158 --> 00:46:58,202
Someone's in there.

690
00:46:58,885 --> 00:47:00,904
I'm saying it loud so she hears me!

691
00:47:00,904 --> 00:47:05,784
I studied film! She didn't even major in it...

692
00:47:05,784 --> 00:47:09,160
- I want to be a director too!
- Stop it.

693
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:13,974
It's my first time, so please help me a lot.

694
00:47:13,974 --> 00:47:16,151
I look forward to working with you.

695
00:47:16,151 --> 00:47:18,466
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

696
00:47:22,843 --> 00:47:24,022
Try this.

697
00:47:24,022 --> 00:47:27,375
Director Woo, come have a drink.

698
00:47:30,412 --> 00:47:32,697
Here, sir.

699
00:47:45,857 --> 00:47:47,574
I'll get going first.

700
00:47:47,574 --> 00:47:49,953
Are you going home? Should I drive you?

701
00:47:49,953 --> 00:47:51,274
I'll take a cab.

702
00:47:51,274 --> 00:47:53,629
Okay. Get home safe.

703
00:47:53,629 --> 00:47:56,362
- Good night.
- Good night.

704
00:47:56,362 --> 00:47:59,312
- Then we'll...
- Where are you going?

705
00:47:59,312 --> 00:48:01,619
Round two!

706
00:48:01,619 --> 00:48:03,675
Round two!

707
00:48:03,675 --> 00:48:05,385
- Round two!
- Oh my...

708
00:48:05,385 --> 00:48:06,982
Round two!

709
00:48:09,911 --> 00:48:11,911
[Jinsusungchan]

710
00:48:24,690 --> 00:48:26,512
When...

711
00:48:26,512 --> 00:48:27,683
When did you get here?

712
00:48:27,683 --> 00:48:29,575
- Director Ryu.
- Yes?

713
00:48:29,575 --> 00:48:34,072
This is the first and last time
I'll explain my decision.

714
00:48:34,072 --> 00:48:35,522
Sorry?

715
00:48:35,522 --> 00:48:37,713
What do you mean?

716
00:48:37,713 --> 00:48:41,154
"Gyeongseong Love Song" was written
by Yi Jae in her senior year.

717
00:48:41,154 --> 00:48:44,992
That's why I left the script meeting
entirely to her.

718
00:48:44,992 --> 00:48:49,285
I decided it made more sense for me
to handle location scouting.

719
00:48:50,455 --> 00:48:52,092
Director Ryu.

720
00:48:52,092 --> 00:48:56,273
Director Ju Yi Jae is doing her job perfectly.

721
00:48:58,502 --> 00:48:59,520
Yeah...

722
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:02,089
Does even hearing that bother you?

723
00:49:02,089 --> 00:49:03,982
Not at all.

724
00:49:04,596 --> 00:49:07,452
Absolutely not.

725
00:49:07,452 --> 00:49:09,749
I'm sorry.

726
00:49:09,749 --> 00:49:12,203
You don't need to apologize to me.

727
00:49:12,816 --> 00:49:15,350
From now on,

728
00:49:15,350 --> 00:49:19,148
let's each do our part and respect each other.

729
00:49:19,148 --> 00:49:20,238
Got it.

730
00:49:20,238 --> 00:49:21,942
Enjoy your meal.

731
00:49:25,599 --> 00:49:27,130
Hey.

732
00:49:28,126 --> 00:49:29,136
Ma'am.

733
00:49:29,136 --> 00:49:31,337
Please put the staff meals on my card.

734
00:49:31,337 --> 00:49:33,712
You're paying for all of them?

735
00:50:01,453 --> 00:50:02,677
<i>No.</i>

736
00:50:02,677 --> 00:50:04,845
<i>Nobody said anything.</i>

737
00:50:04,845 --> 00:50:07,011
<i>Isn't that weird?</i>

738
00:50:07,011 --> 00:50:11,717
<i>No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.</i>

739
00:50:11,717 --> 00:50:13,721
<i>It's true, though!</i>

740
00:50:13,721 --> 00:50:15,523
<i>Calm down...</i>

741
00:50:18,560 --> 00:50:20,539
<i>I'm saying it loud so she hears me!</i>

742
00:50:20,539 --> 00:50:23,240
<i>I studied film! She didn't even...</i>

743
00:50:31,104 --> 00:50:32,914
- Hello?
<i>- Where are you?</i>

744
00:50:32,914 --> 00:50:34,938
<i>We need to talk.</i>

745
00:50:34,938 --> 00:50:36,962
I'm outside your place.

746
00:50:36,962 --> 00:50:39,275
[Jaejae Noodles]

747
00:50:50,256 --> 00:50:51,927
What are you doing?

748
00:50:52,591 --> 00:50:54,156
Watch me.

749
00:50:54,980 --> 00:50:57,726
- Why are you...
- Just watch from there!

750
00:51:01,971 --> 00:51:03,041
See?

751
00:51:03,041 --> 00:51:04,798
I can run like this!

752
00:51:04,798 --> 00:51:06,997
It doesn't hurt at all!

753
00:52:27,812 --> 00:52:33,033
<i>You know how I've lived.</i>

754
00:52:34,902 --> 00:52:39,262
<i>I spent whole days stuck in mudflats.</i>

755
00:52:40,269 --> 00:52:43,312
<i>I climbed countless mountains.</i>

756
00:53:00,109 --> 00:53:02,268
So stop.

757
00:53:03,570 --> 00:53:09,325
Because of you, my scar feels even clearer.

758
00:53:14,293 --> 00:53:17,809
If you're truly sorry,

759
00:53:17,809 --> 00:53:20,499
if you feel that bad for me,

760
00:53:22,239 --> 00:53:25,175
then see this too.

761
00:53:25,949 --> 00:53:28,898
Even after everything, I'm standing here now.

762
00:53:31,083 --> 00:53:33,577
Please understand

763
00:53:34,783 --> 00:53:37,339
what it took to get here.

764
00:53:37,339 --> 00:53:39,203
Please.

765
00:53:41,047 --> 00:53:43,471
I really want to do this well.

766
00:53:43,471 --> 00:53:45,742
I don't want any more regrets.

767
00:53:51,361 --> 00:53:53,497
Help me, Soo Bin.

768
00:53:54,538 --> 00:53:56,984
Help me keep running.

769
00:54:00,160 --> 00:54:01,557
<i>What's your dream?</i>

770
00:54:01,557 --> 00:54:03,782
<i>A film director.</i>

771
00:54:03,782 --> 00:54:05,204
<i>Hurry!</i>

772
00:54:06,220 --> 00:54:08,805
<i>Pretty cool, right?</i>

773
00:54:13,646 --> 00:54:18,220
<i>I'll be a director
who makes films that feel human.</i>

774
00:54:18,220 --> 00:54:20,595
<i>Let's go, Ju Yi Jae!</i>

775
00:54:22,908 --> 00:54:26,111
<i>Let's make a movie together.</i>

776
00:54:26,111 --> 00:54:29,604
<i>Let's do something great.</i>

777
00:54:31,828 --> 00:54:33,389
<i>Romance.</i>

778
00:54:33,389 --> 00:54:35,943
<i>Let's write a romance together.</i>

779
00:54:35,943 --> 00:54:38,319
<i>A really great one.</i>

780
00:54:59,704 --> 00:55:02,384
I always wanted to be like you.

781
00:55:03,554 --> 00:55:06,238
That bright look on your face.

782
00:55:17,192 --> 00:55:20,565
That's why I like you, Yi Jae.

783
00:55:42,339 --> 00:55:44,244
This is what I should've done

784
00:55:44,931 --> 00:55:47,209
when we were 19.

785
00:56:05,616 --> 00:56:09,525
I'll stop here.

786
00:56:11,986 --> 00:56:14,471
So you can shine brighter.

787
00:56:15,247 --> 00:56:21,213
I can't be a stain on your life anymore.

788
00:56:21,213 --> 00:56:22,866
I'm sorry.

789
00:56:23,609 --> 00:56:25,240
No.

790
00:56:27,140 --> 00:56:30,917
I wasn't asking for an apology.

791
00:56:30,917 --> 00:56:33,530
I was asking you to help me.

792
00:56:34,141 --> 00:56:36,293
I'm sorry.

793
00:56:36,918 --> 00:56:39,259
This is all I can do.

794
00:56:40,831 --> 00:56:42,769
What matters is...

795
00:56:42,769 --> 00:56:47,186
we finish the movie together.

796
00:56:48,033 --> 00:56:52,036
But give me some time to sort myself out.

797
00:56:55,666 --> 00:56:58,582
Until the new draft is ready,

798
00:56:58,582 --> 00:57:01,752
I'll work alone at home.

799
00:57:01,752 --> 00:57:03,468
Take care.

800
00:57:06,576 --> 00:57:09,722
Why say it like we're saying goodbye forever?

801
00:57:09,722 --> 00:57:12,304
I guess we are.

802
00:57:12,304 --> 00:57:14,068
To our first love.

803
00:57:14,982 --> 00:57:19,590
Once the new draft comes in,
let's meet as colleagues.

804
00:57:21,551 --> 00:57:24,891
Oh, that kind of goodbye...

805
00:57:27,569 --> 00:57:29,542
Okay.

806
00:57:29,542 --> 00:57:30,962
Bye.

807
00:57:30,962 --> 00:57:32,465
Yi Jae.

808
00:57:32,465 --> 00:57:34,198
Yeah.

809
00:57:34,198 --> 00:57:37,217
See you soon, Director Ju.

810
00:57:37,875 --> 00:57:39,538
Bye.

811
00:58:46,696 --> 00:58:48,806
<i>Director Ju.</i>

812
00:58:48,806 --> 00:58:51,520
<i>I really want to be in this film.</i>

813
00:58:51,520 --> 00:58:52,713
<i>Who's coming?</i>

814
00:58:52,713 --> 00:58:53,837
<i>Sim Yu Geon?</i>

815
00:58:53,837 --> 00:58:55,369
<i>- Soo Bin?
- What do you want?</i>

816
00:58:55,369 --> 00:58:58,507
<i>Give him the role, or drop Ju Yi Jae.</i>

817
00:58:58,507 --> 00:59:01,444
<i>I hate when you show up like this.</i>

818
00:59:01,444 --> 00:59:05,228
<i>Amazing! The vibe changed when he walked in.</i>

819
00:59:05,228 --> 00:59:07,654
<i>- Time flies.
- Waiting for you felt longer...</i>

820
00:59:07,654 --> 00:59:09,041
<i>I should go.</i>

821
00:59:09,041 --> 00:59:11,986
<i>Then what were we back then?</i>

822
00:59:11,986 --> 00:59:14,094
<i>I think it's love.</i>
